From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvgpu: scale: report the rate of a duplicate request

simple_ondemand asks for an arbitrary frequency; the target callback rounds it to a rate of the
GPU's table and returns that rate in *freq, which devfreq accounts. When the rounded rate is the
one already set, the callback returned early with *freq still unrounded, so devfreq looked up a
rate that is not in its table, logged

  devfreq 57000000.gpu: Couldn't update frequency transition information.

and left its time-in-state statistics wrong.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/scale.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/scale.c
@@ -290,8 +290,11 @@
 	rounded_rate = platform->clk_round_rate(dev, local_freq);
 
 	/* Check for duplicate request */
-	if (rounded_rate == g->last_freq)
+	if (rounded_rate == g->last_freq) {
+		/* devfreq accounts *freq, and knows only the table's rates */
+		*freq = rounded_rate;
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (g->ops.clk.get_rate(g, CTRL_CLK_DOMAIN_GPCCLK) == rounded_rate)
 		*freq = rounded_rate;
